retain their own terms; this license grants no additional rights to them.

Personal, educational, internal and ordinary commercial projects, modifications,
and client-specific development/delivery are permitted without a license fee.
You may charge for independent development, design, deployment and maintenance.
A business application, including a paid or multi-tenant SaaS, using the map only
for its own concrete business information or operations and without exposing
general reusable Earth/map capability to its users is not prohibited merely
because it charges fees or subscriptions. Its own business viewing, zooming,
filtering, annotation and reporting do not alone constitute a general reusable
Earth/map capability. This exception does not authorize building, delivering,
operating or maintaining a restricted paid platform for a client, even under a
custom-development contract, one-time delivery or development-service fee.
Free demonstrations, tutorials and sharing remain permitted subject to
attribution and the restrictions below.

Without the author's prior written permission, you may not package, embed,
host, rebrand, redistribute or offer all or part of this work or modifications
as reusable Earth/map capability for development, generation, editing,
configuration, access, embedding, export or reuse, including separately sold
rendering/display components. This covers paid platforms, SaaS, low-code builders,
AI/agent platforms, APIs, Skills, plugins, SDKs, components, templates and resources.
The restriction applies without source delivery or installation on a user's
device, including server-side hosting, remote calls and returned generated or
rendered results. Subscriptions, membership, usage fees, purchasable credits,
paid downloads/licensing, bundled sales and fees included in another service
are covered. When the capability forms part of a paid offering, a free entry,
trial, basic quota, free features or lack of separate pricing does not exempt it.
Splitting functions, contracts or collection of fees across related parties,
partners or arranged intermediaries does not avoid the restriction. Actual
capability and charging arrangements control, not product labels or contract names.
Human or AI-assisted rewrites, language/framework changes, splitting or combining
code remain subject to the terms where they retain protected content or adapt
it; modification percentages or removing attribution do not alone exempt a use.
These terms do not restrict independent implementations that do not use the
protected content, and do not extend software copyright to ideas, processes,
methods or mathematical concepts. Statutory rights that cannot be excluded,
valid historical grants and separate third-party rights are unaffected.

When using, copying, modifying, integrating, delivering or distributing this
work or adaptations retaining its protected content, retain the original author
copyright, attribution, license/SPDX identifiers and source notices in the
corresponding source code. Do not remove, conceal, alter or replace those notices
with another attribution. Splitting, combining, relocating, renaming, translating
or human/AI-assisted rewriting does not remove this obligation. If their original
location cannot be retained, preserve equivalent complete notices at the top of
the source files carrying the retained or adapted protected content. Additional
modifier credits are permitted; identify modifications and do not claim official
authorship, status or endorsement.
The required author attribution is “作者全平台ID：宋夏天Dazzle；公众号：送你整个夏天”,
with the original repository identified above. Attribution in a README,
documentation, about page or release notes is supplementary and must not replace
